From 84c157781a1e459aaaa67efbedcdfdd34ef1ff35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ksooo <kai.sommerfeld@gmx.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 06:32:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [Android] Restart once the previous instance has exited

After quitting, the activity is gone but the process keeps shutting down
for several seconds with its UI thread blocked. Launching the app in that
window showed a grey screen until the process exited and then dropped
back to the launcher.

Once shutdown begins, watch for such launches from a background thread
and hand them over to a helper activity in its own process. It shows a
notice, waits for the main process to exit and then relaunches the app
with the original intent.
---
 cmake/scripts/android/Install.cmake           |   1 +
 .../packaging/xbmc/AndroidManifest.xml.in     |   9 ++
 tools/android/packaging/xbmc/src/Main.java.in |  24 +++
 .../xbmc/src/RestartActivity.java.in          | 149 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../android/packaging/xbmc/src/Splash.java.in |   7 +
 5 files changed, 190 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tools/android/packaging/xbmc/src/RestartActivity.java.in

diff --git a/cmake/scripts/android/Install.cmake b/cmake/scripts/android/Install.cmake
